<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/Woodgrove-Meadows.jpg" alt="A painting of a farm shed at Woodgrove Meadows" width="550" height="441" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Sketch Club Painting at Woodgrove Meadows. 11x14, oil on linen panel. 2015</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Beginning with a&nbsp;<span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">gradated color wash over a</span><span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">&nbsp;simple raw umber block that was already dry,&nbsp;</span><span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">I managed to finish the final layer of this painting in one (long) day.</span></p>
<p><span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">What drew my eye to this scene was the contrast of textures in the foreground against the smooth areas of the sky and shadows; the presence of the figure was more of a bonus.</span></p>
<div><span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">While I left the sky as an intense blue, I softened the colors in the trees to make them recede more into the background although I must admit that it took me a long time to figure out how to do that. &nbsp;I used some color variation in the dark areas to intensify the center of interest around the figure and add mystery - it's an interesting effect that I haven't tried before now. &nbsp;</span></div>
<p style="text-align: left;">&nbsp;</p>